{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And it came to pass at the end.</b> As the Targum renders: 'at the end.' And every term קֵץ is 'end.'" "<b>Upon the river.</b> All other rivers are not called יְאֹרִים except the Nile, because the whole land is made into channels, channels by human hands, and the Nile rises through them and waters them — because rains do not fall in Egypt regularly as in other lands."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 41, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:02:50.018261373Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}